From: Dynamic Devices <engineering@dynamicdevices.co.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] abseil: use portable ordering types

The Foundries worker combines modern Clang with an older host libstdc++.
Abseil's automatic detection sees compiler C++20 support and aliases its
ordering types to std:: ordering types, but that libstdc++ has no <compare>
header. Select Abseil's documented C++11-compatible implementation instead.
This also gives host and target objects the same ordering type configuration.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Foundries host libstdc++ compatibility]

diff --git a/deps/v8/third_party/abseil-cpp/absl/base/options.h b/deps/v8/third_party/abseil-cpp/absl/base/options.h
index caa92e7..81f230a 100644
--- a/deps/v8/third_party/abseil-cpp/absl/base/options.h
+++ b/deps/v8/third_party/abseil-cpp/absl/base/options.h
@@ -204 +204 @@
-#define ABSL_OPTION_USE_STD_ORDERING 2
+#define ABSL_OPTION_USE_STD_ORDERING 0
